think The live edge is the Season G open-media family; the newest rung is image/min_width.rye (the edge-first minimum-width slot). The card and the min_width log named the crux-first next sibling: the LARGEST INSCRIBED disk, the inner bound the family's outer/edge bounds mirror, "likely iterative, a Chebyshev-center read".
think Chose the exact-integer path over the float-iterative one the card anticipated: the chamfer distance field (image/distance.rye, already built) gives every foreground pixel its integer distance to the nearest background pixel, so the deepest pixel IS the center of the largest inscribed disk, its distance the inscribed radius in chamfer units. The DECISION (argmax) is exact integer; only the reported radius (chamfer/3) is f64, exactly as min_enclosing_circle reports its own. Concavity-aware where every convex read is blind -- the honest inner companion.
think Designed the decisive crux convention-safely. The chamfer-inradius and the hull-Euclidean circumradius use different pixel conventions, so a naive "inradius <= circumradius" can flip on a compact square (block chamfer-radius 3.0 vs enclosing radius 2.828). So did NOT assert that inequality. Instead the decisive statement compares two INNER reads to each other (same chamfer units): a solid 5x5 block and a hollow 5x5 RING trace the IDENTICAL outer contour, so convex_hull and min_enclosing_circle read the SAME hull and SAME enclosing circle for both -- yet the inscribed disk shrinks from depth 9 (radius 3) to depth 3 (radius 1). The inner bound SEES the hole the outer bounds cannot tell apart -- mirroring contour's own solid-vs-hollow crux, measured now as inner depth. The inner/outer roundness pairing is shown on the elongated BAR (inradius 1 << enclosing radius 4.12, a 4x gap no convention gap can flip).
obs Predicted every chamfer depth before the metal run (block center 9, ring wall 3, bar 3, dot 3) from the chamfer 3-4 rule cost = 4*min(dx,dy) + 3*|dx-dy|, and all four landed EXACT on the first full run -- no algorithm red, no fixture over-claim. Measurement matched memory this lap because the primitive was hand-traced, not guessed.
obs disk_contains and holds_round_peg keep the exact-integer discipline: membership is dist_orthogonal^2 * squared-distance <= chamfer^2 (the square root cleared by squaring), and peg admission dist_orthogonal * r <= chamfer -- the honest INNER dual of min_enclosing_circle's fits_through_round_hole. No float in any decision.
obs Compose not braid held cleanly: the module owns ONLY the argmax over image/distance.rye's field and the two exact reads; distance owns the chamfer field and its weights, qoi the buffer. The witness imports convex_hull + min_enclosing_circle to PROVE the outer bounds are identical for block and ring, but the module leans on distance alone for its own computation.
